From 2b4cfe8eb7a12c22e9d552be9e77a8c105e47381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:56:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 189/193] probesock: reordering told by the least RTT; the
 buffer back after a probe

- The holes a packet fills are told apart (reordering or loss) at the end
  of the probe, by the least RTT of the connection (TCP_INFO), not by the
  time of its connect: on a busy host the connect took long, the window
  grew, and retransmissions were counted as reordering (the stand under a
  build: 1.6 % counted of 3 %).
- After a probe the connection gets a receive buffer of the system maximum
  (SO_RCVBUFFORCE): a multiplexed transport (gRPC, HTTP/2, xhttp, mux) keeps
  the connection a probe dialed in its pool and carries other connections
  over it, which the window of 16 KB would hold to a crawl.
- The debug line of a probe tells the bytes reordered.
